<title>USA: US cannot let EU subsidies go on forever - Glickman.</title>
<headline>US cannot let EU subsidies go on forever - Glickman.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman on Monday said the United States cannot let European Union wheat subsidies &quot;go on forever&quot; without a response, and urged Congress to back President Clinton's FY98 budget request for $500 million for the Export Enhancement Program.</p>
<p>&quot;I see the Europeans have continued to use some export subsidies in their sales of wheat. We can't let that go on forever without some kind of response,&quot; Glickman told reporters at a briefing on his upcoming trip to South Africa.  </p>
<p>&quot;If we think our producers need it (EEP) to survive and be competitive then we'll use it,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Glickman called for full funding for the export program. Funding for EEP this year was capped at $100 million by Congress.</p>
<p>&quot;I do believe it would be extremely imprudent not to adequately fund the EEP,&quot; Glickman said.</p>
</text>
